Dialogue: 0,0:00:08.41,0:00:12.25,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If ever there were a devilish act\Ncommitted in this world,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:12.33,0:00:14.55,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,this incident would\Ndefinitely have to be it.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:15.05,0:00:16.26,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The devil, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:16.92,0:00:20.93,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We State Alchemists are human weapons in the service of the military.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:21.01,0:00:23.26,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Whenever something comes up,\Nwe are called upon,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:23.35,0:00:25.56,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and if ordered to,\Nwe must dirty our own hands.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:26.39,0:00:28.81,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,From the point of doing this\Nor that with other people's lives,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:28.89,0:00:32.56,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,there's not a huge difference between the position we're in and the actions that Tucker took.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:33.44,0:00:36.65,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That is the reasoning of an adult.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:36.73,0:00:39.28,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But those children are still so...
Dialogue: 0,0:00:42.78,0:00:43.70,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother...
Dialogue: 0,0:00:43.95,0:00:45.62,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother, the Lt. Colonel...
Dialogue: 0,0:00:48.00,0:00:49.29,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's a wasted effort.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:50.66,0:00:55.00,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It is not possible to reconstruct\Na living creature once its life has been lost.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:55.29,0:00:57.05,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Not for any alchemist.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:58.17,0:01:01.88,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Who is it going to please to bring an abortive Chimera back to life?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:02.68,0:01:04.22,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There will be even greater suffering and anguish than this
Dialogue: 0,0:01:04.47,0:01:07.72,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,waiting for you further down the road you have chosen.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:08.18,0:01:11.02,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,As such, you must keep moving forward,\Neven if you have to force yourselves to accept this.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:11.10,0:01:12.81,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Accept this, you say?!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:14.65,0:01:16.90,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There is some purpose you're trying to accomplish, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:17.44,0:01:19.69,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Do you have time\Nto just stand still?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:22.95,0:01:24.16,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,For crying out loud,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:24.24,0:01:26.91,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I won't even be able to get in\Na good bath with my daughter.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:27.41,0:01:28.24,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Here?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:28.33,0:01:29.16,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yes, sir.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:29.66,0:01:32.00,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,From here on, this is a job for\Nthe Investigations Department.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:32.08,0:01:32.92,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Stand aside.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:40.34,0:01:41.26,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This is something awful.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:41.97,0:01:44.97,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Is this the work of that serial killer?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:45.39,0:01:47.26,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That guy specializes in young ladies, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:47.43,0:01:49.56,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What's more, this one\Nhasn't been carved up.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:50.64,0:01:52.27,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's almost as if...
Dialogue: 0,0:01:53.02,0:01:56.27,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,they were blown up from the inside or something, from the look of it.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:59.73,0:02:03.57,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Man cannot obtain anything\Nwithout first sacrificing something.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:04.45,0:02:08.16,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,In order to obtain anything,\Nsomething of equal value is required.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:08.74,0:02:13.25,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That is alchemy's\NLaw of Equivalent Exchange.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:14.41,0:02:19.29,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,At the time, we believed that\Nto be the true way of the world.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:13.24,0:04:14.83,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's a pretty serious look on your face.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:14.99,0:04:17.62,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,For some reason, it feels like I'm at my wit's end.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:18.00,0:04:21.12,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And here I thought I was through wavering all over the place.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:23.38,0:04:24.46,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,So then,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:24.59,0:04:26.59,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,what are these orders?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:28.38,0:04:29.22,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:34.01,0:04:36.89,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Sort out the materials here and organize them,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:37.18,0:04:40.89,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and make yourself completely familiar with the results of Tucker's research.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:40.98,0:04:44.48,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Are you telling me to\Ntake over Tucker's research?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:44.82,0:04:46.78,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He went about it the wrong way,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:46.86,0:04:49.65,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,but there were portions of Tucker's research that have merit for the military.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:50.07,0:04:52.16,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Then you can let Tucker\Ntake care of it, can't you?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:52.82,0:04:53.66,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He's...
Dialogue: 0,0:04:54.53,0:04:55.37,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,dead.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:56.74,0:04:59.62,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Apparently, his guilt was obvious,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:59.96,0:05:02.87,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,so at the discretion of the higher-ups, he was executed.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:05.50,0:05:06.96,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You mean this was covered up!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:07.05,0:05:08.38,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,How could they?!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:08.63,0:05:11.09,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Pledge your loyalty to the military.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:11.34,0:05:14.09,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's the main principle\Ngoverning State Alchemists.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:21.89,0:05:26.48,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Say, it looks like Tucker-san was also doing research on the Philosopher's Stone.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:26.65,0:05:29.40,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Oh? That's nice.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:31.11,0:05:33.74,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,How long are you going to sulk like this, Brother?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:33.91,0:05:38.24,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The Philosopher's Stone is the ultimate secret to us alchemists, you know.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:38.33,0:05:40.25,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It increases your faculty without bound
Dialogue: 0,0:05:40.33,0:05:43.00,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and makes transmutation\Nbeyond principles possible.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:43.12,0:05:45.75,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,In other words, the things that\Nwe weren't able to do could be—
Dialogue: 0,0:05:46.04,0:05:48.25,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That thing is just a legend!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:48.75,0:05:50.26,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's a fairy tale!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:50.76,0:05:54.72,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But if Tucker-san, a State Alchemist, was doing research on it, then...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:54.84,0:05:56.64,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Who gives a damn\Nabout his research?!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:57.05,0:06:00.60,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Al, have you forgotten about Nina?!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:07.36,0:06:08.65,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I cannot permit it.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:08.86,0:06:09.98,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Why not?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:10.28,0:06:13.70,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That serial killer might've done Nina in like that, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:13.78,0:06:15.36,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'll help out in finding him!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:15.86,0:06:17.74,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And the work you were ordered to do?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:18.03,0:06:20.08,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What about analyzing Tucker's research?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:21.66,0:06:23.33,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I don't want to.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:23.41,0:06:25.33,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'll investigate on my own, then.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:25.71,0:06:27.58,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Okay. In that case,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:28.63,0:06:29.92,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,leave that here.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:30.84,0:06:32.09,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I intended to.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:35.63,0:06:36.72,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:38.93,0:06:40.56,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Just a minute!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:40.64,0:06:42.97,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You're not the only one
Dialogue: 0,0:06:40.64,0:06:44.85,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,who's upset over not being able to do anything for Nina, Brother!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:45.02,0:06:46.94,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We're alchemists, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:47.02,0:06:50.19,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Catching criminals isn't\Nsomething that we can do.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:50.27,0:06:54.03,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We do research so that if another girl like Nina \Never comes along who we can save...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:07.58,0:07:08.67,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:09.38,0:07:11.59,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You... You're the guy from the library.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:15.80,0:07:18.89,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If you were able to come\Nand go at the first branch,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:19.01,0:07:21.18,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,does that mean you're\Na State Alchemist?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:21.47,0:07:23.01,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,At the time, yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:23.18,0:07:25.14,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But not anymore.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:25.23,0:07:26.06,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Is that so?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:26.64,0:07:28.06,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You're better off.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:31.86,0:07:35.15,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You're better off, that is...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:36.19,0:07:38.11,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}assuming you don't want to be destroyed by this arm.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:45.83,0:07:48.25,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Ed and Al sure will be surprised!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:48.33,0:07:51.84,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,They'd never expect me, Winry-chan,\Nto come all this way and congratulate them!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:52.54,0:07:53.42,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,All righty!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:55.96,0:07:58.01,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Excuse me, Lt. Hawkeye?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:58.34,0:07:59.34,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's all right.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:59.55,0:08:02.51,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But then, I don't know much about the Philosopher's Stone, either.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:03.35,0:08:06.81,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,At least, I've never heard of it actually existing.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:06.93,0:08:08.94,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I thought it was just a legend.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:09.02,0:08:10.65,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I see...
Dialogue: 0,0:08:11.98,0:08:15.53,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,However, I think you'd be better off\Nnot paying any interest in such a thing.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:16.90,0:08:21.41,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's said that bad things happen to anyone that gets close to the Philosopher's Stone.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:21.49,0:08:25.70,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Oh, you're interested in the \NPhilosopher's Stone, are you?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:27.41,0:08:28.96,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Who is this?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:29.04,0:08:30.79,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Th-This gentleman is...
Dialogue: 0,0:08:32.50,0:08:35.25,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You want to obtain the\NPhilosopher's Stone, do you?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:35.75,0:08:36.59,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yes...
Dialogue: 0,0:08:37.21,0:08:38.59,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,For what reason?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:40.09,0:08:41.01,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,For human—
Dialogue: 0,0:08:41.13,0:08:45.31,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I mean, I want to recover \Nsomething that my brother has lost.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:45.39,0:08:49.06,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Oh? You must think highly of your brother, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:51.19,0:08:56.27,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I don't know any particulars myself,\Nbut there are a lot of people who\Nbelieve in the Philosopher's Stone.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:56.69,0:09:02.28,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What's more, once in a while,\NI hear stories about alchemists\Nwho have succeeded in creating a Philosopher's Stone.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:02.45,0:09:05.74,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Such rumors naturally have a way of gathering around the military.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:06.08,0:09:10.75,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There should be a number of records about it\Nin the first branch of the Central Library.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:10.96,0:09:12.50,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Really?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:12.87,0:09:17.17,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But then, only State Alchemists are allowed to make use of it.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:18.92,0:09:23.34,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,So, a State Alchemist could verify \Nwhether the rumors are true or not.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:29.64,0:09:34.02,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Führer, why would you listen in \Non something like that?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:35.73,0:09:38.86,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's good for the youth\Nto pursue their dreams.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:39.69,0:09:41.95,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Don't you think so, Lieutenant?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:42.40,0:09:43.24,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Sure...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:47.12,0:09:48.62,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,See, I'm right!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:48.70,0:09:50.75,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You think\Nshe's cute too, don't you?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:50.83,0:09:52.79,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Y-Yeah, I guess...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:59.80,0:10:00.96,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What do you think?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:01.67,0:10:04.18,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You think she takes after me?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:04.26,0:10:07.22,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What can I say? Everyone says so!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:07.97,0:10:09.97,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Don't bother me, Pops!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:10.47,0:10:12.77,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There's no need for that kind of talk.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:12.85,0:10:15.98,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Not when I've been showing you the classified analysis of the serial killer.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:16.35,0:10:20.19,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You owe me two. One for the train, and one for your wife's delivery.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:20.28,0:10:21.57,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Oh, yeah?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:21.74,0:10:25.16,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Well, in any case, we're at a standstill.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:25.36,0:10:28.28,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The crimes happen within the city, but there are no witnesses.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:28.37,0:10:30.24,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The bodies are outright sliced up,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:30.33,0:10:33.00,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,but nobody believes that he could do it all in such a short time.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:33.37,0:10:36.67,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Could he have killed them\Nand then brought the bodies around?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:36.88,0:10:39.34,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,How much time has passed from the time of death?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:39.42,0:10:43.01,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Not even the investigators\Nare clear on that very often.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:43.09,0:10:46.93,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But between the military and police,\Nwe've opened up and checked the trunk of every car...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:49.35,0:10:50.51,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,coming into the city.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:50.89,0:10:53.68,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There must be some sort of blind spot.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:53.77,0:10:55.52,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,A car that can hide the bodies,\Nor something...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:55.89,0:10:58.02,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Or maybe it's the work of an alchemist...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:58.69,0:11:01.02,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Alchemists are not murderers!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:05.99,0:11:08.74,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Uh, are you Edward Elric-san?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:09.12,0:11:10.08,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:10.24,0:11:13.20,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There's a visitor to see you at the Headquarters reception desk.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:13.29,0:11:14.12,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,A visitor?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:18.96,0:11:19.79,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Howdy!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:19.88,0:11:21.80,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Thanks, as usual!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:21.88,0:11:22.71,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's all right.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:23.84,0:11:26.30,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,They held the state\Ncertification exams again, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:26.38,0:11:27.22,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Y-Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:27.72,0:11:28.93,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Oh, did you hear?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:29.14,0:11:32.81,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This time, there was a twelve-year-old who passed the test.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:32.89,0:11:33.72,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I hear he just does this with his hands,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:35.18,0:11:37.31,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and just like that, he can transmute.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:37.39,0:11:38.90,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Really?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:39.10,0:11:41.23,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There, the blond one.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:41.98,0:11:43.73,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And he's just a child, too.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:44.28,0:11:47.11,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Oh, come to think of it,\Nwatch out for that one guy.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:47.28,0:11:50.57,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,They say he only\Ncuts up the pretty ones.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:51.07,0:11:53.74,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Oh my, are you worried about me?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:54.16,0:11:55.20,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Sure.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:55.29,0:11:57.16,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I sure hope they catch him soon.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:57.25,0:11:58.25,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You bet.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:58.41,0:12:00.46,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,So, about these incidents...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:00.63,0:12:03.38,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Have you heard anything else?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:07.09,0:12:09.84,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,How long is Ed going to\Nkeep me waiting?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:17.60,0:12:20.23,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's a refrigeration unit!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:21.40,0:12:24.86,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Central sure does have\Nthe latest cars.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:24.94,0:12:28.15,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,How nice!\NI sure would like to dismantle it!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:28.44,0:12:30.66,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm afraid having it dismantled would put me out.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:31.36,0:12:33.07,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm sorry!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:33.16,0:12:34.78,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Is this your truck?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:34.95,0:12:35.91,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's right.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:36.12,0:12:38.37,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This is my\Nfood shop's delivery truck.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:44.46,0:12:45.84,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Is something the matter?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:46.21,0:12:47.92,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If you'd like, would you\Ncare to look inside?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:48.01,0:12:49.80,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\an8}Huh? I can?!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:49.88,0:12:51.93,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Thanks so much!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:57.52,0:12:58.35,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:58.98,0:13:01.52,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I told her to wait right here.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:01.60,0:13:03.10,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's strange...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:04.23,0:13:05.32,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Elric-san?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:13.99,0:13:14.87,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Is this...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:20.25,0:13:21.50,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Winry?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:21.58,0:13:22.42,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:25.54,0:13:27.88,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Was there a car stopped here?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:28.00,0:13:32.97,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yeah, there are always \Nrefrigerated trucks stopping here,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:28.92,0:13:32.97,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,whose dealers serve\Nthe military's cafeteria.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:33.84,0:13:35.26,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Refrigerated truck?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:36.14,0:13:37.76,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Something that could hide a body?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:37.85,0:13:38.77,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It couldn't be...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:39.97,0:13:40.93,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Elric-san?!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:03.08,0:14:04.46,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Hey, are you all right?!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:06.17,0:14:08.38,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Were you kidnapped as well?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:08.92,0:14:10.76,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Over there, there's someone else.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:11.26,0:14:12.22,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There is?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:12.30,0:14:15.22,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Okay, let's take them and get out of here, quick!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:15.89,0:14:18.30,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'll be here with you, \Nso don't worry—
Dialogue: 0,0:14:31.82,0:14:33.11,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Good morning, junior.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:33.36,0:14:35.82,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Why, you!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:37.49,0:14:41.62,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I heard that you can transmute\Nwithout using transmutation circles,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:42.29,0:14:43.25,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,so just to be safe...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:47.17,0:14:48.88,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Let me introduce myself.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:49.29,0:14:51.75,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm the shop's owner, Barry.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:52.17,0:14:53.46,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,A man?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:53.80,0:14:58.18,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,As a reward for making it this far, \Nlet me show you something you'll like.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:07.31,0:15:08.15,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Winry!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:08.69,0:15:12.78,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm about to craftily dissect this little girl.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:13.15,0:15:16.65,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Be sure to watch closely, now,\NMr. State Alchemist.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:16.95,0:15:18.32,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Stop!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:18.49,0:15:19.66,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Why are you doing this?!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:20.24,0:15:21.37,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Why?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:21.74,0:15:24.95,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Well now, because I enjoy it, I suppose.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:26.75,0:15:29.83,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The first person I killed was my wife.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:30.63,0:15:32.71,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We were having some\Npetty argument, you see.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:33.42,0:15:35.63,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Then, without meaning to, I killed her.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:36.59,0:15:39.72,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But then, she cut up so neatly, you know?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:39.80,0:15:44.43,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,After that, I started wanting to \Ncut people up even more neatly.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:44.72,0:15:47.14,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I wanted everyone to see.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:47.27,0:15:50.90,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,How can one person kill another for something like that?!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:51.40,0:15:52.65,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Oh, but they can!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:53.32,0:15:56.65,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Given just the slightest opportunity, a person can kill another.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:55.82,0:15:56.65,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Stay back!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:57.40,0:16:02.03,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If they go off to war, it's even easier for one person to kill another.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:02.41,0:16:03.95,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Why do you suppose that is?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:04.04,0:16:05.24,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I-I don't know.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:08.75,0:16:11.04,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's because people\N{\i1}want{\i0} to kill each other.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:11.38,0:16:17.22,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,On the battlefield, I saw\Na State Alchemist just like you\Nkill other people with ease.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:17.30,0:16:19.18,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Splat! Just like that.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:19.26,0:16:20.09,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,No...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:24.85,0:16:25.68,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,No!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:32.69,0:16:33.52,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Why, you!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:42.07,0:16:42.91,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:03.43,0:17:04.26,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Dammit!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:53.98,0:17:54.81,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Don't!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:59.69,0:18:02.53,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It'll take more than that to kill me.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:05.16,0:18:06.28,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,They're in here!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:07.78,0:18:08.83,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Don't move!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:10.87,0:18:11.70,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Al...
Dialogue: 0,0:18:12.96,0:18:14.04,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother...
Dialogue: 0,0:18:14.54,0:18:15.50,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Does that hurt?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:16.46,0:18:18.34,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I thought I was going to get killed.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:18.50,0:18:21.67,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I really thought that I might die...
Dialogue: 0,0:18:22.55,0:18:24.26,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I was terrified...
Dialogue: 0,0:18:25.05,0:18:27.26,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Terribly scared...
Dialogue: 0,0:18:34.31,0:18:35.69,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Thanks to Hughes-san realizing
Dialogue: 0,0:18:35.77,0:18:41.28,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,that trucks from this same food shop had passed inspections many times,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:41.53,0:18:44.24,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,we somehow managed to get there in time.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:46.03,0:18:50.24,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Afterward, the case of \NBarry the Chopper became famous,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:51.24,0:18:54.16,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and it would be spoken of as Brother's first distinguished achievement.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:58.84,0:18:59.84,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother...
Dialogue: 0,0:19:01.00,0:19:04.09,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The Philosopher's Stone\Nmight really exist.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:04.72,0:19:10.26,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But in order to search for it, you have to be certified as a State Alchemist.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:11.43,0:19:13.18,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Since I don't have a body,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:13.39,0:19:17.02,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I can't really feel the terror you felt,\Nthinking you were going to be killed, Brother.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:17.77,0:19:19.56,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm sure it must've been lonely...
Dialogue: 0,0:19:20.31,0:19:21.23,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and painful...
Dialogue: 0,0:19:23.15,0:19:27.86,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Sure, I want my old body back...\Nto be human again.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:27.95,0:19:29.53,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Once we find the\NPhilosopher's Stone,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:30.24,0:19:35.16,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,even if it means having to go against the flow of the rest of the world,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:31.16,0:19:35.16,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,as though nothing will ever come of it...
Dialogue: 0,0:19:37.04,0:19:39.29,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Having nearly been killed, I realized something...
Dialogue: 0,0:19:40.08,0:19:43.38,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,All I could do was scream.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:43.88,0:19:46.92,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,My mind just went completely blank.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:48.05,0:19:52.51,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I couldn't even bring myself to think there would be anyone to save me.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:53.35,0:19:55.27,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,For all that we're able to do,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:55.47,0:19:58.56,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,we'll have our hands full just trying to get our own bodies back.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:59.19,0:20:00.44,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,To that end,
Dialogue: 0,0:20:00.65,0:20:04.44,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,whether it means being a dog of the military, or cursed as the devil, I don't care...
Dialogue: 0,0:20:05.94,0:20:07.11,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But then,
Dialogue: 0,0:20:07.19,0:20:12.12,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,we really aren't devils, much less gods.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:13.03,0:20:14.54,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We're only human!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:16.12,0:20:21.79,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Tiny, insignificant humans, \Nwho couldn't even save Nina...
Dialogue: 0,0:20:26.38,0:20:28.05,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,A condition, you say?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:28.72,0:20:30.55,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I will obey my duties to the military.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:30.64,0:20:34.85,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,As such, I would like to be told all information there is about the Philosopher's Stone.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:36.22,0:20:40.60,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,When I have no other duties, permit me to search for the Philosopher's Stone.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:40.69,0:20:44.52,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Are you sure you want it to get out that you committed the sin of human transmutation?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:44.73,0:20:49.03,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Your brother will be\Nbrought into the laboratory\Nas an extraordinary\Nexample of transmutation.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:50.86,0:20:54.28,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,At least, that's the way I {\i1}could{\i0}\Npressure you to make sure you stay in line.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:56.87,0:20:58.33,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Okay, very well.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:58.87,0:21:04.17,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But you will report to me everything you find out about the Philosopher's Stone.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:05.71,0:21:08.76,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You have been given\Na title from the Führer.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:09.05,0:21:11.76,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's quite an ironic title, though.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:18.14,0:21:22.65,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\an8}"We give the name 'Fullmetal' to thee,
Dialogue: 0,0:21:22.73,0:21:26.65,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\an8}Edward Elric, in the name of Führer King Bradley."
Dialogue: 0,0:21:28.28,0:21:29.53,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Fullmetal?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:30.03,0:21:34.53,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,State Alchemists are given a silver watch,\Nas well as a second name.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:34.82,0:21:37.54,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The second name that you will bear is "Fullmetal."
Dialogue: 0,0:21:38.16,0:21:40.04,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The Fullmetal Alchemist.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:43.62,0:21:46.38,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I like it. It has an oppressive feel to it.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:46.46,0:21:48.05,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Sure, I'll take on that name!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:49.63,0:21:53.80,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,To celebrate, you're going to treat me\Nto all kinds of delicious things!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:54.14,0:21:55.64,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You've got it backwards, don't you?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:55.89,0:21:58.35,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I fixed your arm, didn't I?
Dialogue: 0,0:22:03.02,0:22:07.90,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother, I heard that the serial killer \Ndidn't have anything to do with Nina.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:08.19,0:22:11.44,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,No, he seems to have an alibi for that night.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:12.28,0:22:15.70,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Then, I wonder who it was that wiped out Nina like that...
Dialogue: 0,0:23:38.91,0:23:40.45,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Fullmetal Alchemist{\i0}...
Dialogue: 0,0:23:40.53,0:23:44.25,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Episode 9: "The Dog of the Military's\NSilver Watch"
Dialogue: 0,0:23:45.00,0:23:47.96,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I knew what it would mean to become a State Alchemist
Dialogue: 0,0:23:48.58,0:23:52.55,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,from the very beginning,\NAl...
